---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Services
permalink: /services/
description: "Exactly what JaniCrew cleans in each area of your building: reception, restrooms, carpets, floors, offices and break rooms, plus day porter, floor care, carpet cleaning and window washing."
eyebrow: Commercial cleaning services
heading: Exactly what we clean, room by room.
lede: "A JaniCrew scope is a checklist, not a promise. This is what each area includes, and it is the same list your local owner walks through with you on site."
heroImage: conferenceTable
heroLabel: Crew member wiping a boardroom table
---
{% include "partials/hero.njk" %}

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="container">
    <blockquote class="pull-quote">
      "{{ janicrew.company.openingLine }}."
      <cite>The line at the top of every JaniCrew quote sheet</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight" id="scope">
  <div class="container">
    {% set areaImages = {
      "Reception / Lobby": "lobbyMopping",
      "Restrooms": "restroomSink",
      "Carpets": "officeVacuuming",
      "Floors": "floorBuffer",
      "Offices": "deskWipe",
      "Break Room": "supplyCaddy"
    } %}
    {% for a in janicrew.services.coreScope %}{% if a.tasks.length %}
    <article class="area area--media" id="{{ a.area | slugify }}">
      <div class="area__head">
        <h2>{{ a.area }}</h2>
        {% if a.rationale %}<p>{{ a.rationale }}</p>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <ul class="checklist checklist--2">
        {% for t in a.tasks %}<li>{{ t }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
      <div>
        {% set img = images | slot(areaImages[a.area]) %}
        {% set slotLabel = a.area + " photo" %}
        {% set ratio = "4/3" %}
        {% set eager = false %}
        {% include "partials/image-slot.njk" %}
      </div>
    </article>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    <article class="area" id="additional-specifications">
      <div class="area__head">
        <h2>Additional specifications</h2>
        <p>Tailored to your industry regulations</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Health codes, infection control, after-hours access, background checks, product restrictions: whatever your industry requires goes into the written scope before we start. See the <a href="/industries/">industries we serve</a> for what we focus on in each kind of building.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt" id="additional-services">
  <div class="container split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Additional services</p>
      <h2>When you need more than the routine.</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        {% for s in janicrew.services.additional %}{% if s != "Other" %}
        <li>{{ s }}</li>
        {% endif %}{% endfor %}
        <li>Something else? Ask. If we cannot do it, we will say so.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid--2">
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Schedules</h3>
        <p>{{ janicrew.services.schedules | joinTasks(", ") | replace("Other", "or a schedule of your own") }}. Most accounts run after hours; day porter service covers you during the day.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel panel--yellow">
        <h3>How pricing works</h3>
        <p>You get a monthly estimate in writing, based on the scope and the schedule, after a 5-10 minute walkthrough. There is no rate card because no two buildings are the same.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% include "partials/cta-band.njk" %}
